WEBVTT

00:35.928 --> 00:37.759
Oh, Peter, you're selling your anvil?

00:37.864 --> 00:40.196
Yeah, I've had a lot of good times
with this thing.

00:42.434 --> 00:43.867
(CHUCKLING)

00:43.969 --> 00:45.767
Oh, a dollar!

00:46.104 --> 00:48.698
- Hey, there, Chris.
- Hi, Mr. Herbert.

00:48.807 --> 00:51.298
- Selling your old hand-me-downs?
- Yep.

00:51.409 --> 00:54.206
You got anything
you used to wear in the summertime?

00:54.311 --> 00:57.804
- Just these old shorts.
- Sweet Jesus.

00:57.949 --> 01:01.042
You know, Brian. I'm looking forward
to getting rid of some of this crap.

01:01.151 --> 01:04.746
<i>Like this movie,
Stimy Gruffin, The Untold Story.</i>

01:04.855 --> 01:08.813
It's not a movie at all, Brian.
Just three episodes, back to back.

01:08.925 --> 01:10.290
This thing is an insult.

01:10.393 --> 01:12.657
Well, that might be
overstating things a little.

01:12.762 --> 01:15.025
It's a middle finger to the fans,
is what it is.

01:15.130 --> 01:17.122
I tell you, Fox should be...

01:18.233 --> 01:20.326
- Give you $1 for this.
- Sold.

01:23.605 --> 01:26.573
Brian, where's Rupert?
I just left him here to watch my things.

01:26.674 --> 01:27.606
Uh-oh.

01:27.708 --> 01:29.574
- What?
- Nothing, I haven't seen him.

01:29.678 --> 01:33.977
It's not like him to wander off.
Rupert? Rupert! Oh, no.

01:34.082 --> 01:36.242
- What if he's been kidnapped?
- Well, let's just calm down.

01:36.350 --> 01:38.408
I've got to save him, Brian.
What if he's dead?

01:38.518 --> 01:40.282
I don't think I can handle a funeral.

01:41.923 --> 01:46.018
Of all the souls I have encountered
in my travels, his was the most

01:47.761 --> 01:48.887
human.

01:49.029 --> 01:50.291
MAN: Orders.

01:50.562 --> 01:52.189
<i>(BAGPIPE PLAYING
AMAZING GRACE)</i>

02:20.023 --> 02:22.423
Holy crap. Evel Knievel gloves.

02:22.526 --> 02:23.993
I bet I could do a wheelie with these.

02:24.094 --> 02:25.857
- How much for the gloves?
- Peter, those are yours.

02:25.963 --> 02:29.626
$10, $2, $7, $4, $5.50, $10. Sold.

02:29.733 --> 02:33.065
Sucker. I would've gone to $15, easy.
I am so stupid.

02:33.736 --> 02:34.929
Awesome.

02:35.604 --> 02:38.596
Peter, you can't drive a car over that.
You're gonna get hurt.

02:38.707 --> 02:41.802
Lois, I don't come down to Burger King
and tell you how to do your job.

02:41.911 --> 02:42.877
Peter, I don't work at Burger...

02:42.978 --> 02:45.845
"I don't work at Burger..." I'm busy.

02:45.947 --> 02:49.178
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have some death to defy.

02:59.660 --> 03:03.288
Wow. This is just like what happened with
Matthew Broderick, except no one's dead.

03:06.266 --> 03:07.926
(DOORBELL RINGING)

03:08.534 --> 03:10.229
- Hey, Joe.
- Good morning, Peter.

03:10.336 --> 03:13.134
- I'm here to revoke your driver's license.
- What? Why?

03:13.239 --> 03:15.832
We got reckless driving,
disturbing the peace,

03:15.941 --> 03:18.570
plus the driver of one of those other cars
was a virgin

03:18.678 --> 03:21.305
whose hymen was busted by the airbag,
so rape.

03:21.413 --> 03:23.937
Okay, well, I guess
you can take my license.

03:24.048 --> 03:26.381
- 'Course, it's all the way up here.
- Peter, knock it off. Give it to me.

03:26.485 --> 03:28.247
- Right here. Here you go, Officer.
- Give me the damn license.

03:28.352 --> 03:29.410
Don't you want it? Here.

03:29.520 --> 03:31.181
- This is in poor taste, Peter.
- Having some trouble there?

03:31.288 --> 03:33.188
- You're starting to piss me off.
- All you gotta do is take it.

03:33.290 --> 03:34.723
- You're starting to piss me off!
- It's right here.

03:38.029 --> 03:41.293
Oh, man, this sucks. I got no license.
I can't go anywhere.

03:41.398 --> 03:44.424
Well, this is your own fault, Peter,
and if you want my opinion,

03:44.534 --> 03:47.525
a little time away from the bar
will do you some good.

03:47.636 --> 03:50.105
I'll show her. I'll just go to another bar.

03:50.206 --> 03:52.070
<i>MAN ON TV: We now return to Cheers.</i>

03:52.174 --> 03:53.471
<i>- Norm.
- Norm.</i>

03:53.575 --> 03:55.167
And Peter. Yeah.

03:55.310 --> 03:57.904
<i>- How's life in the fast lane, Mr. Peterson?
- Griffin.</i>

03:58.013 --> 03:59.604
<i>I can't find the on-ramp, Woody.</i>

03:59.714 --> 04:03.844
He was talking to me, Norm. Quit stealing
my punch lines, you fat drunk.

04:03.951 --> 04:07.546
That show stopped being funny
after Kirstie Alley ate Shelley Long.

04:07.655 --> 04:11.522
Oh, man, now I can't even watch TV.
What the hell am I gonna do all day?

04:11.625 --> 04:13.890
That's all right, that's okay.
I don't need TV.

04:13.995 --> 04:16.019
I'll just make my own sitcom in my head.

04:16.129 --> 04:18.962
And I'll give it
an upbeat '80s sitcom theme.

04:22.135 --> 04:24.830
<i>This time around I'm staying at home</i>

04:24.937 --> 04:28.031
<i>And things are gonna get better</i>

04:28.140 --> 04:31.075
<i>Settling in, loving my wife</i>

04:31.177 --> 04:34.305
<i>But then I got that letter</i>

04:34.480 --> 04:37.039
<i>My black son, my black son</i>

04:37.382 --> 04:40.613
<i>Now each day my heart is getting bigger</i>

04:40.718 --> 04:45.178
<i>Don't even remember
sleeping with that lady, but I did</i>

04:45.290 --> 04:48.224
<i>My black son, he's coming to stay</i>

04:48.459 --> 04:53.590
<i>My black son, he's making each day</i>

04:53.730 --> 04:55.288
<i>The best that he can</i>

04:55.398 --> 04:57.026
<i>Also, he's a ninja</i>

05:01.304 --> 05:02.636
What the hell's wrong with you?

05:02.739 --> 05:08.142
I'm so distraught over losing Rupert
I needed something to calm me down.

05:08.244 --> 05:10.075
This is an entire bottle of NyQuil.

05:10.179 --> 05:13.306
I know, and it's doing wonders.

05:13.415 --> 05:17.181
Come here, puss. Come here.

05:17.285 --> 05:20.914
Come here, puss. Here, puss.

05:21.857 --> 05:24.450
- What are you doing?
- Calling the cat.

05:24.558 --> 05:27.357
We don't have a cat. That's a throw pillow.

05:27.562 --> 05:29.256
(CRYING)

05:37.804 --> 05:39.965
Why have you brought me
to the toy store, Brian?

05:40.073 --> 05:41.506
I'm buying you another Rupert.

05:41.608 --> 05:42.905
Hey, this one's cute, huh?

05:43.009 --> 05:45.910
And if we buy it,
they save a real gorilla in the wild.

05:46.012 --> 05:49.105
And if we don't, they kill one.
Wow, these guys are playing hardball.

05:49.214 --> 05:52.980
You can't just take some Korean-made
velveteen primate and call it Rupert.

05:53.085 --> 05:56.713
Now, come on, this is all time we could
be using to find Rupert's kidnappers.

05:56.821 --> 05:59.881
Look, I may as well come clean with you.

05:59.991 --> 06:01.583
Rupert wasn't kidnapped.

06:01.692 --> 06:04.786
I accidentally sold him at the yard sale.

06:04.896 --> 06:06.864
You son of a bitch!

06:07.064 --> 06:08.496
(WAILING)

06:13.870 --> 06:16.202
Come on, Stewie,
I'm really sorry. It was an accident.

06:16.306 --> 06:18.934
Damn you, Brian.
How could you sell Rupert?

06:19.042 --> 06:22.136
What you've done is more horrible
than sex with Sharon Stone.

06:22.479 --> 06:23.945
Wow, that was great.

06:24.079 --> 06:25.979
One minute I'm filling up at Chevron,

06:26.081 --> 06:28.072
and the next
I'm having sex with Sharon Stone.

06:28.184 --> 06:30.652
Yeah. Now comes the best part.

06:38.860 --> 06:42.728
- Get out of the fridge, Peter.
- There is no Peter, only Zuul.

06:42.830 --> 06:45.662
- I said get out of the fridge.
- All right, all right.

06:45.766 --> 06:49.497
Jeez, Lois, I'm just trying to amuse myself,
since I don't have a damn driver's license.

06:49.603 --> 06:53.095
Look, Peter, it's getting a little annoying
having you around the house all the time.

06:53.207 --> 06:56.369
So you'll be happy to know
I got you your own personal driver.

06:56.475 --> 06:59.104
My own driver?
Holy crap, that's awesome.

06:59.213 --> 07:01.703
- Where is he?
- She's right here, Peter.

07:01.814 --> 07:03.111
- Meg?
- Yeah, Dad.

07:03.216 --> 07:05.309
I don't mind driving you around
till you get your license back.

07:05.418 --> 07:07.818
What? Lois, this is the best you could do?

07:07.920 --> 07:10.787
Well, it was either Meg
or a talking monkey smoking a cigar,

07:10.890 --> 07:12.652
but I didn't think you'd like that.

07:12.824 --> 07:15.088
I've already accepted another job.

07:15.260 --> 07:18.229
Lois, you picked the opposite thing
that I would like.

07:18.430 --> 07:21.023
It's all right.
I would've driven you bananas.

07:21.198 --> 07:23.963
Oh, and he makes jokes. Nice going, Lois.

07:24.602 --> 07:26.069
Dad, are you ready?

07:29.273 --> 07:32.003
- What exactly are you trying to do?
- It's very simple, Brian.

07:32.109 --> 07:35.237
I've taken DNA from the dollar bill
you were paid for Rupert.

07:35.346 --> 07:38.337
Now to check that DNA
against the federal database.

07:38.548 --> 07:39.708
We have a match.

07:39.816 --> 07:42.785
"Stanford Cordray, 89 Spooner Street."

07:42.885 --> 07:45.079
Well, that's only a few blocks away.
Let's go!

07:49.758 --> 07:50.816
(DOORBELL RINGING)

07:50.926 --> 07:52.359
Hello? Hello?

07:54.396 --> 07:56.387
It can't be. This house is deserted.

07:57.565 --> 07:59.591
He moved. He's gone.

07:59.735 --> 08:04.898
- Rupert's gone.
- Wait a minute. Look! The moving truck.

08:05.005 --> 08:07.702
- We're not too late.
- Hey! Hey!

08:09.643 --> 08:11.440
Can I help you, gentlemen?

08:11.545 --> 08:13.136
Follow that truck.

08:13.580 --> 08:15.241
Didn't you hear me?
I said, "Follow that truck."

08:15.348 --> 08:19.284
Oh, I heard you.
What I didn't hear was "please."

08:19.386 --> 08:21.353
- Please follow the truck.
- Please follow the truck.

08:23.990 --> 08:26.480
I always enjoy traveling companions.

08:26.592 --> 08:30.585
Let's play 20 questions. Am I Bo Bice?
Yes, I am.

08:30.696 --> 08:33.528
Well played, worthy adversary.

08:39.504 --> 08:42.234
We're gaining on him. I'm coming, Rupert.

08:45.609 --> 08:48.976
- I'm sorry, but I can go no further.
- What? Why not?

08:49.079 --> 08:50.103
If I enter Connecticut,

08:50.213 --> 08:54.012
I'm entering every state
that Connecticut's ever been with.

08:54.116 --> 08:56.085
Good luck, brave travelers.

08:58.721 --> 09:01.189
No! We were so close.

09:05.860 --> 09:09.421
I say, what a bit of serendipity.
Now we've got that fellow's address.

09:09.531 --> 09:11.761
Let's see. "Aspen, Colorado."

09:11.866 --> 09:14.391
Well, you can forget that.
We're not going all the way to Aspen.

09:14.502 --> 09:16.766
What? But I can't leave Rupert to perish.

09:16.871 --> 09:19.305
For the rest of my life,
I'll be as lonely as Pat Robertson

09:19.407 --> 09:21.533
and Jerry Falwell, after the rapture.

09:21.809 --> 09:24.243
Damn it, Jerry,
why are we the only ones still here?

09:24.345 --> 09:26.245
I don't know. We hated all the right things.

09:26.347 --> 09:27.678
Now there's nothing left to hate.

09:27.781 --> 09:30.010
- I'm gonna hate that rock.
- No, I'm gonna hate that rock.

09:30.116 --> 09:31.243
Let's both hate that rock.

09:31.352 --> 09:33.410
- I hate you.
- I hate you, too.

09:37.022 --> 09:38.047
Look, Stewie.

09:38.157 --> 09:40.853
Don't you think at some point
you're going to have to let Rupert go?

09:40.960 --> 09:42.859
I mean, you are getting a little old
to have a teddy bear.

09:42.961 --> 09:43.951
Brian, I'm one.

09:44.063 --> 09:45.051
- Still?
- What?

09:45.163 --> 09:47.961
Look, I'm not going to Colorado.
I'm turning around and going home.

09:48.066 --> 09:49.590
Fine, then. I'll go by myself.

09:49.701 --> 09:51.464
See you from the back of my milk carton.

09:51.570 --> 09:54.663
Want that on your conscience, Brian?
Try explaining this to Lois.

09:54.772 --> 09:56.104
You'll wind up in a dumpster

09:56.208 --> 09:58.573
with a bunch of slow,
unadoptable greyhounds.

09:58.676 --> 10:01.008
Don't joke about that.
That's like the holocaust to us.

10:01.112 --> 10:03.410
<i>Yeah, well, when greyhounds
start running the New York Times,</i>

10:03.514 --> 10:05.481
and the World Bank,
I'll be more inclined to believe you.

10:05.582 --> 10:08.074
- Now, are you coming or not?
- Fine.

10:11.554 --> 10:16.014
<i>Take to the highway
Won't you lend me your name</i>

10:16.126 --> 10:17.888
- Who sings that song?
- James Taylor.

10:17.993 --> 10:19.085
Yeah, let's keep it that way.

10:20.530 --> 10:21.518
This sucks.

10:21.630 --> 10:24.098
Can you believe I'm stuck with Meg
driving me around?

10:24.199 --> 10:26.190
Dad, it's just you and me in the car.

10:26.301 --> 10:29.428
Yeah, don't remind me.
It's bad enough I got a suspended license.

10:29.537 --> 10:32.005
I gotta ride around town
with Stinky McPoop-Pants.

10:32.107 --> 10:35.269
- I want apple juice.
- Dad, you left your apple juice at home.

10:35.376 --> 10:37.673
I want apple juice!

10:37.778 --> 10:40.748
- You wanna watch SpongeBob?
- Yes.

10:40.848 --> 10:42.508
With apple juice.

10:42.616 --> 10:47.519
<i>C- A-M-P-F-l-R-E S-O-N-G song
C- A-M-P-F-l-R-E S-O-N-G song</i>

10:48.722 --> 10:50.018
SpongeBob.

10:50.724 --> 10:51.816
(CHUCKLING)

10:55.494 --> 10:56.792
Thanks for the ride, Bandit.

10:56.897 --> 11:02.333
Good luck tapping some of that
hot, hot Sally Field tail.

11:02.434 --> 11:05.268
Knock it off.
I don't like it any more than you do.

11:06.337 --> 11:07.497
Where the hell are we?

11:10.375 --> 11:14.071
Oh, this is history right here, Brian.
Gettysburg. Billy Yanks.

11:14.178 --> 11:18.376
The 20th Maine. So many lives lost.
All in pursuit of the ideal that

11:18.482 --> 11:21.747
no man should be subjugated
because of the color of his skin.

11:21.852 --> 11:26.083
These boys paid the ultimate price here.
For equality. For humanity.

11:26.722 --> 11:28.884
- You're welcome.
- I'm sorry?

11:28.992 --> 11:31.289
I'm just saying,
make it worth our while, you know?

11:31.394 --> 11:34.761
We wrote a pretty big check
for you folks here, so...

11:34.864 --> 11:38.060
You know, whatever. It's fine. It's fine.
Doesn't matter. Just...

11:38.166 --> 11:40.294
I just hope you're making the best
of what we gave you here.

11:40.403 --> 11:43.132
I would say that
given the events that preceded it,

11:43.238 --> 11:45.968
the couple hundred years or so,
maybe we're about even.

11:46.074 --> 11:47.632
Yeah, no, no. We gave more.

11:51.245 --> 11:53.441
Hey, Cleveland, who would you rather do?

11:53.548 --> 11:57.415
Queen Latifah or Halle Berry,
but she's been dead for six hours?

11:57.518 --> 12:00.214
Oh, man, that's a tough one.

12:00.321 --> 12:01.345
What did she die of?

12:01.455 --> 12:04.720
I've seen some bodies
that have been dead for six hours.

12:04.825 --> 12:05.950
Some of them aren't too bad.

12:06.059 --> 12:07.356
Oh, then Halle Berry.

12:07.460 --> 12:10.258
God, will you guys
just shut up back there?

12:10.363 --> 12:11.830
(ALL SNICKERING)

12:12.832 --> 12:15.231
Gross! Would you stop it? Stop it!

12:15.601 --> 12:17.502
Hey, guys, check this out.

12:20.539 --> 12:23.975
- Hey, Meg, don't be such a hothead.
- What?

12:24.076 --> 12:27.704
- Hey, Meg, you sure look hot today.
- What?

12:27.812 --> 12:30.280
Hey, Meg, I lit your scalp on fire.

12:30.381 --> 12:31.541
(SCREAMING)

12:31.649 --> 12:33.480
Don't worry, I'll put it out.

12:35.152 --> 12:37.017
(GROANING ANGRILY)

12:39.723 --> 12:42.487
What the hell is your problem,
you dumb bimbo?

12:42.826 --> 12:43.986
(GROWLING)

12:44.427 --> 12:46.053
Oh! Oh, God, stop!

12:46.462 --> 12:48.328
(SCREAMING)

12:53.236 --> 12:56.363
Meg, that was awesome.

13:12.987 --> 13:14.214
If we wanna get to Aspen,

13:14.321 --> 13:16.346
we're gonna have to get over
those mountains somehow.

13:18.892 --> 13:21.292
Excuse me, how much is it
to rent a helicopter?

13:21.395 --> 13:24.125
It's $10 an hour.
But there's a $100,000 deposit.

13:24.231 --> 13:26.222
Oh, God. Looks like we're walking.

13:26.332 --> 13:29.860
Wait a minute, it says here
you accept cash, check or a jaunty tune.

13:29.970 --> 13:32.301
Well, this rental agreement
was drafted back when

13:32.405 --> 13:34.463
musicals were culturally relevant.

13:34.573 --> 13:36.804
Unfortunately, that's no longer the case.

13:36.909 --> 13:40.036
Well, I can prove to you
that's a whole lot of nonsense.

13:41.847 --> 13:46.249
<i>You may think that song and dance
is dated, boring and dry</i>

13:46.351 --> 13:50.684
<i>But you might just learn to like it
if you give it a try</i>

13:50.788 --> 13:54.622
<i>You could laugh and sing and dance
as gaily as an elf</i>

13:54.725 --> 13:59.058
<i>But just in case you don't believe me
Ask the man himself</i>

13:59.162 --> 14:01.427
Mr. Kelly? Will you show us?

14:01.532 --> 14:03.260
- I'll show you.
- Let's do it.

14:03.366 --> 14:04.856
<i>Good
One, two, three, four</i>

14:04.968 --> 14:05.935
<i>One, two, three, four</i>

14:06.035 --> 14:08.026
<i>- One, two, three
- One, two, three</i>

14:08.171 --> 14:09.763
(BOTH SINGING)

14:10.006 --> 14:12.372
- You see?
- It's easy.

15:45.360 --> 15:47.554
Look at me. I'm dancing.

16:02.843 --> 16:04.776
Okay, you can have the helicopter.

16:08.981 --> 16:13.212
Brian, be careful 'cause the mountains
are the same color as the sky.

16:13.318 --> 16:14.307
- What?
- I said,

16:14.419 --> 16:17.786
"Be careful 'cause the mountains
are the same color as the..."

16:17.889 --> 16:19.446
(SCREAMING)

16:20.826 --> 16:23.817
- What the hell was that?
- I'm practicing my comedy crash.

16:23.928 --> 16:26.727
Well, keep it down 'cause I'm trying to...

16:26.832 --> 16:28.196
(BOTH SCREAMING)

16:43.879 --> 16:45.438
(LAUGHING)

16:46.816 --> 16:48.715
(BOTH SCREAMING)

16:52.020 --> 16:56.046
STEWIE: Lmagine the dance I'm gonna
have to do to get our security deposit back.

17:02.363 --> 17:03.762
(PANTING)

17:04.332 --> 17:06.664
Oh, my God. Brian, look.

17:07.368 --> 17:09.028
It's Aspen. We made it.

17:09.136 --> 17:11.798
Well, it looks like you're gonna
be reunited with Rupert after all.

17:11.905 --> 17:14.897
And just in time, too.
I can't keep my teeth from chattering.

17:15.008 --> 17:15.975
(CHATTERING)

17:16.109 --> 17:17.098
Isn't that fun?

17:17.210 --> 17:20.110
I got these at Jack's Joke Shop
in South Attleboro, Massachusetts.

17:20.212 --> 17:22.977
Remember, if it ain't funny,
it ain't worth jack.

17:23.450 --> 17:24.416
Bitch.

17:27.286 --> 17:30.187
Why, you should have seen
what our amazing freaking daughter did

17:30.289 --> 17:32.256
to that guy, Lois. She kicked his ass.

17:32.357 --> 17:34.258
It was like what life did to Dana Plato.

17:34.360 --> 17:38.159
Meg, how could you do that?
You should call that man and apologize.

17:38.263 --> 17:40.731
Hey, hey, hey,
don't you talk to her like that.

17:40.832 --> 17:43.062
Meg's as cool as the other side
of the pillow.

17:45.402 --> 17:48.132
- Billy Dee Williams.
- Hello, Peter.

17:48.238 --> 17:52.766
Welcome to the cool side of the pillow.
You've had a hard day.

17:52.876 --> 17:57.107
Rest that weary head of yours
and drift on off to dreamland.

17:58.381 --> 18:00.975
Works every time.

18:02.051 --> 18:04.849
Well, this is the place. Looks pretty fancy.

18:05.955 --> 18:07.013
(DOORBELL RINGING)

18:07.156 --> 18:10.488
- Can I help you?
- Yes, my name's Brian.

18:10.592 --> 18:12.082
Look, to make a long story short,

18:12.194 --> 18:15.493
I accidentally sold you a teddy bear
back in Rhode Island,

18:15.597 --> 18:18.532
and I kind of need it back.

18:20.367 --> 18:23.360
- Rupert! It's Rupert.
- Stanford, who is it?

18:23.471 --> 18:25.438
It's nothing, dear. I'll handle it.

18:25.539 --> 18:28.939
I'm sorry, but that bear belongs to Timmy.
Now, please leave.

18:31.045 --> 18:34.480
- Wait, wait, how about a ski-off?
- What?

18:34.581 --> 18:37.015
You heard me.
First one down the mountain wins.

18:37.116 --> 18:41.017
- Lf I win, I get Rupert.
- Interesting. What do I get if I win?

18:41.119 --> 18:43.748
- My dog.
- What can he do?

18:45.657 --> 18:49.218
If you put peanut butter anywhere
on your body, he'll lick it off.

18:50.128 --> 18:51.959
Anywhere.

18:53.030 --> 18:55.966
Well, I did go to Choate.
All right, it's a deal.

19:19.990 --> 19:22.514
You know, Dad, it's been really great
hanging out with you.

19:22.625 --> 19:25.492
I know there's probably a million things
you'd rather be doing.

19:25.594 --> 19:28.324
Are you kidding, Meg?
I've had more fun with you than I did

19:28.429 --> 19:31.490
<i>going to see Lost in Translation
with Cleveland and Quagmire.</i>

19:32.901 --> 19:36.564
- What do you think he whispered to her?
- I'll bet it was just right.

19:36.938 --> 19:40.998
Look, I know sometimes I give you
a hard time. You know, calling you names,

19:41.108 --> 19:44.669
reading your diary, farting in your cereal
when you go to get milk

19:44.778 --> 19:48.145
and then laughing,
"She doesn't know she's eating my fart".

19:48.248 --> 19:53.378
But, you know, Meg, I'm starting to realize
I got a really wonderful daughter.

19:53.486 --> 19:54.749
Thanks, Dad.

19:54.855 --> 19:58.756
Peter, good news. Your suspension is up.
You can have your license back.

19:59.458 --> 20:03.588
You mean it? I'm free?
No more getting driven around? Sweet.

20:04.230 --> 20:06.720
So, I guess this means
you don't need me anymore.

20:06.832 --> 20:09.356
You'll probably go back
to treating me like crap, huh?

20:09.467 --> 20:12.402
Well, maybe just to keep up appearances
in front of the family.

20:12.504 --> 20:13.869
You know, peer pressure and all that.

20:13.972 --> 20:17.771
But from now on, Meg,
you and me are secret best friends.

20:18.275 --> 20:21.267
- Who wants a glass of fresh lemonade?
- Not me.

20:21.412 --> 20:24.108
What I want is a fresh glass
of better daughter.

20:24.214 --> 20:25.181
(GLASS SHATTERING)

20:25.349 --> 20:26.373
Hey.

20:37.694 --> 20:39.662
Stewie, do you really think
you can beat this guy?

20:39.762 --> 20:42.628
Trust me, Brian, I've got
a few tricks up my sleeve.

20:52.007 --> 20:55.237
Oh, no, if only I had rockets in my skis.

20:55.376 --> 20:58.004
Oh, wait, I totally have rockets in my skis.

21:03.884 --> 21:07.011
And now I just sit back,
relax and watch my progress.

21:12.892 --> 21:15.622
- Tea, sir?
- Oh, thank you, Crone.

21:15.729 --> 21:17.423
You're so pleasant.

21:17.896 --> 21:20.990
- Would you like to check on the race, sir?
- Yes, why not?

21:22.668 --> 21:24.295
(SCREAMING)

21:28.240 --> 21:29.672
(LAUGHING)

21:33.478 --> 21:35.378
Well, that's it, I suppose.

21:35.480 --> 21:39.610
Listen, I'm really sorry, Stewie.
I know how much Rupert meant to you.

21:39.717 --> 21:42.776
I don't know, Brian.
Maybe this is a sign that you were right.

21:42.886 --> 21:45.582
Maybe I am getting too old for Rupert.

21:46.189 --> 21:49.123
I guess I've just got to let him go.

21:49.225 --> 21:51.922
Wow, that's very grown-up of you, Stewie.

21:52.029 --> 21:56.158
Hey, dog, let's go.
My dad won you fair and square.

21:56.265 --> 21:58.130
You're not really gonna live with them,
are you?

21:58.234 --> 21:59.201
No.

21:59.301 --> 22:01.359
- You are not really over Rupert, are you?
- No.

22:01.469 --> 22:04.064
- That's what I thought.
- Oh, Crone.

22:05.840 --> 22:07.603
(SCREAMING)

22:08.943 --> 22:11.138
- How are we gonna get out of here?
- You still got the starting gun?

22:11.246 --> 22:12.213
- Yeah.
- Give it to me.

22:14.381 --> 22:17.578
Get out of the fucking car!
Get out of the fucking car right now, man!

22:17.684 --> 22:19.982
- Get out of the fucking car! Do it, do it!
- Oh, my God.

22:20.087 --> 22:21.679
- I'll do whatever you want!
- I'll fucking kill you!

22:21.789 --> 22:23.416
Get out of the fucking car!

22:24.391 --> 22:29.090
BRIAN: Did we just carjack someone?
STEWIE: We sure did, Brian. We sure did.

22:29.091 --> 23:30.091
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru